      "writtenOn": "2025-02-13T21:16:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The rationale for using `module_param` makes sense, and I\u0027ve moved to using that.\n\nThanks for pointing out the `immediately` option. What is the rationale for adding this? We\u0027re trying to deprecate ashmem\u0027s unpinning feature since it hasn\u0027t proven to be beneficial, so I do not think we should extend it via this new behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "243f2afa_6612abf0",
      "revId": "4af1481d7e015b44701afb3a1bacabde175bac85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "35bb66db_edcc0d72",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/ashmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 984,
      "author": {
        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-14T08:54:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d prefer to avoid module_param for several reasons:\n\n* The Rust driver unregisters the shrinker when the option is changed, so a simple boolean option isn\u0027t enough on the Rust side. We need to trigger an actual callback when it\u0027s changed.\n* Doing that from a module parameter is more tricky because module parameters can be set before the module is initialized, so I need special logic to not touch the shrinker if the option is changed before the module is initialized.\n* I\u0027ve been told by many people [including Greg](https://lore.kernel.org/all/2024121309-lethargic-ended-5f99@gregkh/) that module parameters are discouraged and should be avoided in favor of sysfs.\n\nAs for the `immediately` option, I added it as an alternative option we could try if removing unpinning turned out to not be a good option on dogfood. The idea is to translate the `UNPIN` ioctl to `fallocate(FALLOC_FL_PUNCH_HOLE | FALLOC_FL_KEEP_SIZE)` instead of a no-op. But I\u0027m happy to drop it if we don\u0027t think we will need it.",
      "parentUuid": "767e7058_b83db16e",
      "revId": "4af1481d7e015b44701afb3a1bacabde175bac85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
